message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Strain-Tensor Eigenvalue Decomposition and Intermediate Alignment in 3D Navier–Stokes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Frohman
    given-names: Benjamin Stanley
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7068-3718"
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Texas, United States
    email: frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-strain-eigenvalue"
keywords:
  - strain-rate tensor
  - eigenvalue decomposition
  - vortex stretching
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for a short algebraic note on the eigenvalue
  decomposition of the symmetric, trace-free strain-rate tensor of a
  divergence-free field, together with a Lean 4 skeleton. The Lean file
  records the trace-sum identity for the eigenvalues and states the
  intermediate-alignment rearrangement, which remains unproved (sorry).
  The note is pointwise and unconditional; it does not prove integrability
  of the L^∞ strain norm, Hypothesis B, or the Clay Navier–Stokes problem.
  A kernel check is not a PDE or physical proof.
